      "id": "5wrlbi4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly categorized into communicable, non-communicable, and deficiency diseases.",
        "Communicable diseases are caused by pathogens such as bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa.",
        "Deficiency diseases arise from a prolonged lack of specific essential vitamins or minerals in the diet.",
        "The immune system provides defense via innate (present from birth) and acquired (developed) immunity.",
        "Vaccination activates the body's adaptive immunity to protect against specific pathogens."
      ],
      "id": "4e0fuxy"
    },
